{"name":"Pink Slip","hex":"#d58d8a","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"pink slip","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A notice of termination of employment.","The title document for an automobile."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To terminate the employment of."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pink_slip"}],"entries":[{"title":"Vehicle title","blocks":[{"text":"In the United States, the certificate of title for a vehicle is a legal form, establishing a person or business as the legal owner of a vehicle. Vehicle titles in the U.S. are commonly issued by the Secretary of State in the state the vehicle was purchased by the Department of Motor Vehicles (DMV)."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/Zulass.jpg/330px-Zulass.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vehicle_title","wikidata":"Q1392800"},{"title":"Termination of employment","blocks":[{"text":"Termination of employment or separation of employment is an employee's departure from a job and the end of their time with an employer. Termination may be voluntary on the employee's part (resignation), or it may be at the hands of the employer, often in the form of dismissal or a layoff. Dismissal or firing is usually thought to be the employee's fault, whereas a layoff is generally done for business reasons outside the employee's performance."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/1909_Tyee_-_Faculty_Foot.jpg/330px-1909_Tyee_-_Faculty_Foot.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Termination_of_employment","wikidata":"Q685744"},{"title":"Pink","blocks":[{"text":"Pink is a pale tint of red or rose, the color of the pink flower. It was first used as a color name in the late 17th century. A combination of pink and white is associated with innocence, whereas a combination of pink 